OL,3,GNEWSADrugs running was like 'a paper
OL,4,Around' for exploited son, mum says
OL,5,
OL,6,FA mother whose son was groomed by a
OL,7,Fgang at the age of 13 before being
OL,8,Ftaken into care claims the local
OL,9,Fauthority housed him "right in the
OL,10,Fcentre of exploitation", despite
OL,11,Frepeated pleas for help.
OL,13,FWithin months of being recruited, she
OL,14,Fsaid her son was being forced to
OL,15,Fdeliver drugs in Grimsby for up to 36
OL,16,Fhours at a time ` a "job" he got as
OL,17,Feasily as "a paper round".
OL,19,FThe woman, who we are not identifying,
OL,20,Fsaid it took two years for North East
OL,21,FLincolnshire Council (NELC) to move her
OL,22,Fson to safety.
OL,23,APub: 12-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
